          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at 9 years of age. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately once per month. The epilepsy is drug-resistant.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Brivaracetam\n- Lamotrigine\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately one focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizure per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. The etiology is genetic, associated with a pathogenic PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A.\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen of brivaracetam and lamotrigine. Continue monitoring seizure frequency.",
